course: dictionary
lesson: 1327
title: A caller
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A caller is a person who makes a telephone call. Read the words around it: «The caller said she was from the bank» tells you someone is on the phone. The word also means someone who visits a house for a short time, so a caller can be at your door too.
explain: Look for clues. «Caller ID shows who is phoning» means your phone can show the name or number of the caller before you answer. If you do not know the number, the caller may be a stranger.
explain: Read on for the last meaning. At a bingo game or a barn dance, the caller is the person who calls out the numbers or the dance steps. Swap in your meaning: «The bingo caller read out number twelve» still makes sense.
fact: A caller is a person who makes a telephone call, or who visits a house for a short time.
fact: «Caller ID» shows the name or number of the person who is phoning.
fact: «Unknown callers» are people you do not know, and they can be scammers.
fact: In bingo or a barn dance, the caller calls out numbers or dance moves.
fact: Never give a caller your bank card number, and tell a grown-up about any strange call.
exercise: «The caller said she was from the bank.» What is a caller in this sentence? | A person who sells cakes at a fair | A bell that rings in a shop | *A person who makes a telephone call | A kind of bird
exercise: In a bingo game, what does the caller do? | Counts the money | Plays the numbers on a card | *Calls out the numbers | Wins the prize
exercise: Why should you never give a caller your bank card number? | Because the caller is always a friend | Because it makes the phone ring | *Because it may be a scam | Because bank cards are too small to read
test: «Do not let a caller in unless a grown-up says it is OK.» Where might the caller be? | Inside the bingo card | *At the front door | In the bath | Under the bed
test: Caller ID shows who is phoning. What does it show? | *The name or number of the person phoning | A map of your street | The price of a call | The weather
exam: Ella's phone shows an unknown caller asking, «Is your mum home?» What is the best thing for Ella to do? | Give the caller her bank card number to check it | Say yes, Mum is home and I am alone | *Let a grown-up answer and do not say she is home alone | Tell the caller her address and when her mum will be back
